From 5c083f585133bb5a6bbd2508f60d79227a22d3a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:54:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Sea ice: [sea_ice] evp_substeps, EVP diagnostics output, and
 an EVP convergence test
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ClimaSeaIce's adaptive EVP (v0.7.2) moves the stresses about 1/α of the way to their plastic values per substep, with α
set locally between 50 and 300, and NumericalEarth runs it with 150 substeps: where α exceeds the number of substeps
the ice may resist less than its strength allows. This tests whether the solver converges.

- [sea_ice] evp_substeps (default 150) is passed to sea_ice_dynamics as SplitExplicitSolver(grid; substeps).
- [output] evp_diagnostics = true writes daily averages of α, the ice strength P and the deformation rate Δ to
  arctic_evp.jld2.
- config_smoke_test_evp.toml: 100 km, 4 days, 300 substeps, with the EVP output.
- config_evp_dec2005_n150/300/600/1200.toml: 2 days from GLORYS on 1 Dec 2005, as the hindcast twin otherwise (no
  online transports, no scorecard), differing only in evp_substeps.
- analysis/evp_convergence.jl: compares the runs' last daily averages with the first config's (the most substeps), by
  region: mean ice speed, RMS and max of the velocity difference, median α, share of cells with α > N/3 and the mean
  exp(-N/α); evp_convergence.md and evp_convergence.png.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Abhhvmt8meskhHGBgsw6yN
